Z||000000||BOSTITCH||09-23-1999||02:16 PM||||Iam stroking my 2.8 figured that more fuel to air ratio would help. I'am not sure if these injector from the 3.1 will work the amount of fuel pressure.||||reg||14
Z||000001||CRAGAR||09-23-1999||04:19 PM||||I've got a 3.1 with my old 2.8 MPFI system installed.  I added the adjustable fuel pressure regulator (per FOCOA recommendation) and cranked up the pressure to 48 psi @ WOT and it runs great.  I don't believe that the 3.1 injectors are necessary.  Spennd the injector money on headers!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric||09-23-1999||07:08 PM||||Where did you get the fuel pressure regulator?  I am going to put my new 3.1 rebuild back into the car within the next few weeks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||09-23-1999||08:45 PM||||I'm curious about something. What does your O2 sensor read at wide open throttle? <P>Increasing the fuel pressure increases the fuel, but that's not necessarily what you want. If the O2 reads above 800-850mV at WOT and redline, more pressure is not needed.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||09-23-1999||08:54 PM||||Your putting nearly 50PSI on all that old plumbing? I hope you are being followed around by a fire truck.||||reg||4
Z||000005||CRAGAR||09-24-1999||03:38 PM||||The fuel pressure regulator came with the "kit" that I purchased from FOCOA to do the 2.8 to 3.1 engine swap.  I know that Jegs and Summit Racing also sell this adjustable fuel pressure regulator separately.  As for the O2 readings, I plan on checking those out this weekend.  I believe that the stock pressure spec goes up to 42 or 44 psi; and I recall at least one other Fiero guy recommending 48 psi.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cooter||09-24-1999||09:44 PM||||Why not just run the injectors for the 3.1 in the 2.8 intake? This seems like a more logical choice due to the fact that your 2.8 injectors are probably high mileage and the ones from the 3.1 are newer and probably better matched and less likely to be clogged. Since the ecm reverts to the fuel map at WOT, wouldn't injectors sized for the engine stand a better chance of supplying the right amount of fuel without a regulator?||||reg||1
